{"name":"Dig It","hex":"#8e6e57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dig","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Digo."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move hard-packed earth out of the way, especially downward to make a hole with a shovel. Or to drill, or the like, through rocks, roads, or the like. More generally, to make any similar hole by moving material out of the way.","To get by digging; to take from the ground; often with up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dig"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dig It (Klaus Schulze album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dig It is the thirteenth album by Klaus Schulze. It was originally released in 1980, and in 2005 was the sixth Schulze album reissued by Revisited Records. It is Schulze's first fully digital recording. The 2005 reissue includes a bonus DVD with the video recording of the 1980 performance at Ars Electronica, which was previously released as audio on The Ultimate Edition (2000)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Klaus_Schulze_Dig_It.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dig_It_(Klaus_Schulze_album)","wikidata":"Q3419850"},{"title":"Dig It!","blocks":[{"text":"Dig It! is a jazz album by The Red Garland Quintet, recorded in 1957 and 1958 but not released on the Prestige label as PRLP 7229 until 1962."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3f/GarlandDig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dig_It!","wikidata":"Q3027722"},{"title":"Dig It (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Dig It  is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Yoshidamaru. It began serialization in Kodansha's seinen manga magazine Monthly Afternoon in April 2025."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Dig_It_manga_volume_1_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dig_It_(manga)","wikidata":"Q137010213"},{"title":"Digging","blocks":[{"text":"Digging, also referred to as excavation, is the process of using some implement such as claws, hands, manual tools or heavy equipment, to remove material from a solid surface, usually soil, sand or rock on the surface of Earth. Digging is actually the combination of two processes, the first being the breaking or cutting of the surface, and the second being the removal and relocation of the material found there. In a simple digging situation, this may be accomplished in a single motion, with the digging implement being used to break the surface and immediately fling the material away from the hole or other structure being dug."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cavar_%2826999245241%29.jpg/330px-Cavar_%2826999245241%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digging","wikidata":"Q4232202"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Zeus%2C_Digging_For_China.jpg/500px-Zeus%2C_Digging_For_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Zeus%2C_Digging_For_China.jpg/1280px-Zeus%2C_Digging_For_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Zeus%2C_Digging_For_China.jpg/500px-Zeus%2C_Digging_For_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dog digging on a beach.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZeus%2C_Digging_For_China.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Hunterian_Psalter_c._1170_digging.jpg/330px-Hunterian_Psalter_c._1170_digging.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten